  "$comment": "DEVELOPMENT descriptor for the speak task (handler litert.speak), not in the bundled catalog and not in the repo yet. Files listed at commit d4662d891f9bf54b3d93432610d0d296d229e026; bytes and sha256 of the repo's files come from the Hub's LFS listing. g2p/dp_g2p_matcha_fp16.tflite, g2p/g2p_dict.txt.gz and g2p/g2p_meta.json are copies of litert-community/Matcha-TTS@8d650e79 and g2p/symbols.json is the symbol list of the LiteRT text_to_speech_streaming sample's config.json; none of the four is in the repo at this commit (bytes and sha256 from the local copies), so this descriptor resolves only with the files side-loaded. 'revision' is read by tools/hfmodels_descriptor.py only; the SDK ignores it. The device gate (SpeakDeviceTest) passes this descriptor explicitly. fp32 is the card's 'deploy fp32'; fp16 is the sample's choice (half the size). speed_priors are the publisher's say.py factors; the SDK multiplies speed by them as say.py does. xnnpack: the predictor runs without the XNNPACK delegate, the prosody and vocoder graphs with it (the handler's default too): on a Galaxy S26 (2026-10-03, fp32) the peak RSS after the load was 334 MB instead of 624 MB and the median synthesis 301 ms instead of 288 ms, with the same frames. Verified on a Galaxy S26 SM-S942Q (Android 16 BP4A.251205.006), LiteRT 2.2.0, 2026-10-03: fp32 and fp16 on cpu passed the speak gate with this descriptor's files, fp32 also with the predictor without XNNPACK and the speed priors as above, fp16 only with the earlier handler (no speed priors, XNNPACK on all three graphs) (see verification/2026-10-03-RFGL80R6A6H-BP4A.251205.006-voice.json and tested-runtime-matrix.json, speak).",
